{"author":{"id":"86dc3c885e4fa466d19699d4a5e74c240f1c9d6b23f4e62ea2d2d8e359bd1711"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790714415,"nonce":"URa4XQ5zb2PXIG7c3MjNSouzpo8=","title":"Browse and reopen sketches from the current project","message":"\u003c!-- ABOUTME: Defines the desktop Sketches gallery for saved personal sketch bundles. --\u003e\n\u003c!-- ABOUTME: Covers current-project discovery, safe presentation, and reopening saved sketches. --\u003e\n\n# Browse and reopen sketches from the current project\n\n## Parent\n\n02e51b7 / https://github.com/ff6347/giclang/issues/84\n\n## What to build\n\nAdd a desktop-only gallery labelled exactly **Sketches**, distinct from immutable Examples. Discover bundles only in the sketchbook belonging to the currently configured projects folder. Show a sketch only when it has a saved source and a valid description with `enabled: true`; sort by `order`, then title. Render user-authored Markdown safely, and show a placeholder when an eligible sketch has no thumbnail. Selecting a card opens its actual saved source and description through the one-document workflow with the normal discard guard. Refresh from saved files after successful saves, project-folder changes, and application restart; isolate malformed bundles. This slice delivers stories 18–25 and integrates stories 8, 11, 13, and 27.\n\nUser stories: 18–25; integrates stories 8, 11, 13, and 27.\n\nRelated context only: broad requests 948a98c and 0ac47e5. This slice does not replace, close, or modify those issues.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The desktop IDE provides a gallery labelled exactly **Sketches**, clearly distinct from immutable **Examples**. The browser/PWA does not provide this native-folder gallery.\n- [ ] Discovery is limited to the sketchbook under the currently configured projects folder; it does not scan prior project folders, arbitrary opened-file locations, or other directories.\n- [ ] A gallery entry requires an associated saved source and a valid saved description with `enabled: true`. Validate metadata with the same schema as bundled examples: nonempty string `title`, finite numeric `order`, boolean `enabled`, and string-list `categories` and `tags`; do not blindly pass user Markdown through a trusted bundled-HTML compiler. Sketches without descriptions or with `enabled: false` are hidden; a broken GIC source remains eligible and openable.\n- [ ] Cards use saved title and description, display a saved thumbnail or a placeholder when no thumbnail exists, and sort by numeric `order` followed by title. A thumbnail is not required for eligibility.\n- [ ] User-authored Markdown is rendered as untrusted content and cannot execute arbitrary script or gain unrestricted file access; no arbitrary script access is exposed through its presentation.\n- [ ] Selecting a card opens the real saved source and description in the existing one-document workflow, without making an immutable example copy. The ordinary unsaved-change/discard guard applies, including when only description metadata or body is dirty.\n- [ ] Gallery contents and visibility refresh after successful saves and configured projects-folder changes, and are rebuilt from saved files after application restart. Unsaved description edits do not change saved gallery visibility.\n- [ ] Missing, malformed, or unreadable metadata in one bundle does not break discovery of unrelated valid sketches. Discovery does not repair, overwrite, or delete unreadable user files.\n- [ ] Automated native integration tests use real temporary project folders and files. Cover current-folder scoping, no-description and disabled exclusion, broken-source eligibility, order/title sorting, missing-thumbnail placeholder eligibility, selecting/reopening actual source and description, refresh/restart discovery, malformed-bundle isolation, and preservation of unrelated files; do not mock filesystem operations.\n- [ ] Automated shared Playwright tests drive the real editor to verify only the underlying shared document-switch/discard behavior and description isolation. They do not claim to exercise native Sketches gallery selection, gallery discard protection, or gallery metadata restoration. Do not use hidden DOM state or a test-only desktop bridge.\n- [ ] Packaged macOS acceptance uses a real configured projects folder to save and discover sketches, verify filters and sorting, select a gallery card, and confirm the real native workflow opens its saved source and restores its saved description metadata. Exercise the actual gallery selection discard guard with description-only dirty edits. Change the projects folder, restart and verify discovery, and confirm malformed bundles do not prevent valid entries from appearing.\n- [ ] Packaged macOS acceptance presents malicious user-authored Markdown through the real gallery and verifies it is safely rendered, with no arbitrary script execution or unrestricted file access; do not substitute a test-only bridge for this evidence.\n- [ ] Bundled Examples remain immutable and are not modified by personal gallery operations.\n\n## Blocked by\n\ngit-bug `e132361` — Author, save, and reopen sketch descriptions.","files":null}]}